WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.064 --> 00:00:16.325
I wanted to get away that very night.

2
00:00:17.205 --> 00:00:20.467
I hoped to rejoin Jim so we could continue down the river.

3
00:00:21.387 --> 00:00:26.509
Later, after the king and the duke had gone away, I would send all the money back to

4
00:00:26.569 --> 00:00:27.169
Mary Jane.

5
00:00:28.390 --> 00:00:33.212
I waited until the house was quiet, except for the snores coming from the king's room.

6
00:00:35.144 --> 00:00:38.205
I crept downstairs and passed by the parlor door.

7
00:00:39.485 --> 00:00:42.506
One candle was burning in there, and I could see the coffin.

8
00:00:43.646 --> 00:00:48.108
I tried to open the front door, but it was locked and I didn't have the key.

9
00:00:49.148 --> 00:00:53.729
While I was thinking about what to do next, I heard someone coming down the stairs.

10
00:00:55.290 --> 00:00:56.650
I hurried into the parlor.

11
00:00:57.290 --> 00:00:58.951
Where could I hide the money bag?

12
00:00:59.931 --> 00:01:03.432
The coffin lid was partly open, so I shoved the bag in there.

13
00:01:04.604 --> 00:01:08.548
I accidentally touched Peter's cold hands, which made me shiver.

14
00:01:09.528 --> 00:01:13.432
I quickly hid behind the door just as Mary Jane came into the room.

15
00:01:15.173 --> 00:01:17.876
She sat beside the coffin and cried softly.

16
00:01:18.776 --> 00:01:21.579
Her back was to me, and I snuck out of the room.

17
00:01:22.580 --> 00:01:25.943
I couldn't get out of the house now, so I went back up to bed.

18
00:01:26.903 --> 00:01:32.848
I felt very worried, but if the money stayed where it was, everything would be all right.

19
00:01:32.868 --> 00:01:35.230
I would run away tomorrow and go back to Jim.

20
00:01:36.772 --> 00:01:41.736
When we were a hundred kilometers down the river, I could write a letter to Mary Jane and

21
00:01:41.816 --> 00:01:43.998
tell her the money was buried with her uncle.

22
00:01:44.979 --> 00:01:47.401
But I didn't think things would go that smoothly.

23
00:01:48.583 --> 00:01:53.547
What if someone at the funeral decided to take a last look at Peter and noticed the money

24
00:01:53.567 --> 00:01:58.692
bag? Then the king and the duke would find a way to steal it from Mary Jane again.

25
00:02:00.388 --> 00:02:03.271
All through the funeral the next morning, I was scared.

26
00:02:04.112 --> 00:02:06.374
Would someone find the money bag in the coffin?

27
00:02:07.235 --> 00:02:10.758
But no one did, and Peter Wilks was buried in the cemetery.

28
00:02:11.839 --> 00:02:15.963
I just wished I could be sure the money was really in the coffin with him.

29
00:02:16.904 --> 00:02:21.468
I worried that someone might have gone into the parlor late in the night and taken it.

30
00:02:24.944 --> 00:02:30.406
Meanwhile, the king announced that he would be holding an auction of Peter Wilks' property in two days.

31
00:02:31.486 --> 00:02:34.207
He and his brother had to get back to England, he said.

32
00:02:35.127 --> 00:02:39.488
The lying scoundrel also said that he would take the sisters to England with him.

33
00:02:41.028 --> 00:02:43.669
Poor Mary Jane and her sisters began to pack.

34
00:02:44.770 --> 00:02:49.411
I knew he wouldn't be taking them anywhere, that he and the duke would run away as soon

35
00:02:49.451 --> 00:02:50.471
as the auction was over.

36
00:02:51.491 --> 00:02:55.633
I longed to tell Mary Jane the truth, but I was afraid of what the king and the

37
00:02:55.693 --> 00:02:56.633
duke would do to me.

38
00:02:58.153 --> 00:03:00.614
Then something even worse happened.

39
00:03:01.174 --> 00:03:03.155
Two slave traders arrived in town.

40
00:03:04.035 --> 00:03:06.476
The king sold the family's black slaves to them.

41
00:03:07.276 --> 00:03:10.918
He sold two sons to one trader and their mother to the other trader.

42
00:03:11.858 --> 00:03:14.879
The slaves were very upset as they were being taken away.

43
00:03:16.019 --> 00:03:18.440
Mary Jane and her sisters cried and cried.

44
00:03:19.536 --> 00:03:24.479
Many people in town said that it was a terrible thing to separate a slave family this way.

45
00:03:25.600 --> 00:03:29.983
They began to think that Harvey and William weren't as nice as they had thought.

46
00:03:31.544 --> 00:03:35.907
The next morning, the king and the duke came up to the attic and shook me awake.

47
00:03:35.927 --> 00:03:40.110
"Were you in my room last night or the night before?"

48
00:03:40.750 --> 00:03:41.631
the king demanded.

49
00:03:42.592 --> 00:03:45.554
I understood at once that they knew the money bag was gone.

50
00:03:45.574 --> 00:03:47.935
"Why no, Your Majesty!"

51
00:03:48.636 --> 00:03:48.956
I said.

52
00:03:50.012 --> 00:03:52.053
"Did you see anyone else go in there?"

53
00:03:52.073 --> 00:03:57.836
"Well, I might have seen the slaves go in there to clean up," I lied, thinking fast.

54
00:03:58.817 --> 00:04:04.120
After that, the king and the duke believed that the slaves had stolen the money and they stopped

55
00:04:04.180 --> 00:04:04.860
searching for it.

56
00:04:05.941 --> 00:04:10.243
I knew the black slaves were already far away, where the king couldn't harm them.

57
00:04:12.584 --> 00:04:16.706
As I went downstairs for breakfast, I saw Mary Jane packing her trunk.

58
00:04:17.767 --> 00:04:21.213
She looked so unhappy that I couldn't bear it any longer.

59
00:04:22.254 --> 00:04:23.855
I decided to tell her the truth.

60
00:04:25.076 --> 00:04:28.819
I told her how the king and the duke had met the young man on the boat and

61
00:04:28.880 --> 00:04:34.104
how, after listening to him, they had decided to pretend to be Peter's brothers.

62
00:04:35.125 --> 00:04:37.306
I told her they were thieves and liars.

63
00:04:38.728 --> 00:04:41.690
She believed me and her eyes blazed with anger.

64
00:04:43.572 --> 00:04:48.616
She wanted to have them arrested right away, but I asked her to wait until the next day.

65
00:04:49.840 --> 00:04:52.341
I explained that I needed to get away first.

66
00:04:53.422 --> 00:04:57.544
I couldn't tell her why, but said that I had to help another person who needed me.

67
00:04:58.724 --> 00:05:03.967
I was pretty sure that when Mary Jane told the townspeople about the scoundrels, they would believe her.

68
00:05:04.987 --> 00:05:09.729
But, in case she needed more proof, I told her she could write to the mayor of Bricksville

69
00:05:10.710 --> 00:05:14.792
and tell him that the men who had staged the Royal Nonesuch were in her town.

70
00:05:16.104 --> 00:05:19.926
The mayor would be happy to tell everyone that the two men were crooks.

71
00:05:19.946 --> 00:05:22.888
"And there's one more thing," I said.

72
00:05:22.908 --> 00:05:24.248
"The bag of money."

73
00:05:24.268 --> 00:05:27.790
"Well, those scoundrels have that," she said.

74
00:05:27.810 --> 00:05:30.372
"I was foolish, and I gave it to them."

75
00:05:30.392 --> 00:05:33.694
"No, they don't have it," I said.

76
00:05:33.714 --> 00:05:35.715
"I took it from them to give to you.

77
00:05:36.755 --> 00:05:38.756
I don't have it now, but I know where it is."

78
00:05:40.657 --> 00:05:45.280
At that point, Mary Jane gave me a big hug, which made my face go red.
